# Frontend: Nuxt 4 and Vue 3

`{{ fp }}app/`: pages, components (`components/`), composables, styles (`assets/`), constants
(`app/utils/constants.ts`){% if backend == 'django' %}, API types generated in `app/types/api.d.ts` (`ion repo contract`){% endif %}.
Run: `ion repo dev`; check: `ion repo check` (ESLint, `nuxt typecheck`).

## Code

- **[STRICT-TS]** Strict TypeScript in every `.ts` and `<script setup lang="ts">`.
- **[NO-ANY]** No `any`: `unknown`, then a type narrowing.
- **[ASYNC-AWAIT]** `async/await` with `try/catch` only; `.then().catch()` chains are banned.
- **[MODERN-VUE]** Vue 3.5 / Nuxt 4 APIs: `defineModel()` for `v-model`, `useTemplateRef()` for
  refs, reactive destructured props, `useFetch` / `useAsyncData` with an explicit key. No
  Options API.
- **[EXPLICIT-IMPORTS]** The project's components are imported explicitly
  (`import UiButton from '~/components/ui/UiButton.vue'`): their auto-import is off in
  `nuxt.config.ts`. Only Nuxt's own (`NuxtLink`, `NuxtImg`, `ClientOnly`…) stay automatic.
{%- if backend in ['django', 'fastapi'] %}
- **[API-CALLS]** Components and pages never call the API directly: they go through a composable
  of their domain{% if backend == 'django' %}, which goes through `useApi()`, whose routes, bodies and responses are
  typed by `openapi.json`. No `$fetch` nor `useApi()` in a `.vue` (ESLint rule){% else %}, which validates the response before
  returning it{% endif %}.
{%- endif %}
- **[UI-STATES]** Every screen that loads data handles the three states explicitly: loading,
  error (an understandable message, never "Error." alone) and empty list.
- **[ACCESSIBILITY]** Every field has an associated `<label>`, every icon button an `aria-label`,
  every informative image an `alt`. Everything works with the keyboard and focus stays visible.
- **[TEST-DENSITY]** The front's test density (lines of tests per thousand lines of code) never
  drops: its floor in `charter.toml` is raised as it goes up (floor).

## Styling

- **[STYLE-1]** No `<style>` nor `<style scoped>` tag in a `.vue` file (components and pages): a
  `.vue` holds only markup (utility classes) and TypeScript (checked).
- **[STYLE-2]** **Tailwind by default (95 % of cases)**, right in the template: layout and sizes,
  backgrounds, text, borders, radii, shadows, typography, interactive states (`hover:`, `focus:`,
  `disabled:`, `active:`), breakpoints. **Separate CSS by exception (5 %)**, required as soon as
  one of these holds: a multi-step animation (any `@keyframes`); a native browser element
  (`::-webkit-scrollbar`, cursors); a black-box third-party component whose HTML cannot be
  changed (a chart or a map drawn by a library); an unreadable class string that fights the
  engine ([STYLE-5]).
- **[STYLE-3]** `app/assets/css/main.css` is the only file `nuxt.config.ts` references. It
  imports Tailwind, then `tokens.css` (the **only definition of the theme tokens**: `@theme`,
  `:root`: fonts, colours, chart palettes, sizes, letter spacing, radii, shadows, layers,
  breakpoints, widths, durations), then the isolates in alphabetical order, and keeps only what
  holds for the whole product (shared `@utility`, page and layout transitions, a global
  `prefers-reduced-motion` rule). A component writes the class of a token, never an arbitrary
  value that copies it (`text-[0.7rem]`, `z-[120]`). A new isolate is added to `main.css` in the
  same commit.
- **[STYLE-4]** Every rule of an isolate sits under **one parent selector** used as a namespace
  (`.map-tooltip` in `map.css`): no bare element selector (`div`, `span`) outside a parent class;
  the inside of a third-party component is reached by CSS nesting or `:deep()` under that parent.
- **[STYLE-5]** Banned: bursts of arbitrary classes (`[&_div:nth-child(3)]:px-4`): turn them into
  a class of the matching isolate; `@apply` to rebuild a component (that is a Vue component's
  job), except a `@utility` of `main.css` naming a token the whole product shares; `!important`,
  except to override a third-party library that forces it.
{%- if level >= 2 %}

## Performance and quality

- **[CORE-WEB-VITALS]** Budgets at the 75th percentile, on mobile: **LCP < 2.5 s**,
  **INP < 200 ms**, **CLS < 0.1**. A regression beyond them blocks the release.
- **[JS-BUDGET]** A JavaScript budget per page, checked at build time; every heavy library
  (chart engine, map) is loaded on demand (`defineAsyncComponent`, dynamic import).
- **[MODERN-IMAGES]** Images in AVIF/WebP, sized (`width`/`height`), loaded lazily below the
  first screen.
- **[E2E-JOURNEYS]** Critical journeys have a Playwright end-to-end test, run in CI against a full
  stack.
- **[AUTOMATED-ACCESSIBILITY]** Main pages pass an automated `axe-core` check; target
  **WCAG 2.2 level AA**.
{%- endif %}
